  "description": "YAVYIG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C79 H139 N2 O42 P6 Sm5,5(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm5 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.927-3.979 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.83-108.99°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm5(μ3-OH)(NO3)2(dipp)6(CH3OH)7(H2O)4]·5CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
